Apple VM's change to StikJIT 1.9.0 (MPL-2.0), applied after stikjit-high-address.patch by
scripts/build_jit_deps.sh: Configuration.deviceAddress may be an IPv6 address as well as an IPv4
one. StikJIT built the RemotePairing tunnel's socket address with inet_pton(AF_INET) only, so an
IPv6 address became 0.0.0.0; it now passes a sockaddr_in6 and its length to idevice's
tunnel_create_rppairing, which accepts both, and an address that is neither is an error instead
of 0.0.0.0. Built-in JIT uses it to reach the device through the user's own VPN
(docs/builtin-jit.md, "Using your own VPN instead of LocalDevVPN").

